en.description:
OUR COMPANY

Zurich promotes diversity in all its forms! We invite #women, #black people, #PWD, #LGBTQIA+ individuals, and #senior professionals to apply for our vacancies!

Imagine working at a company that truly cares about its employees, clients, stakeholders, and the entire community involved. Imagine working at a company committed to doing the right thing, aiming to be the best insurance provider in the world!

Zurich is one of the leading insurance companies globally and one of the few operating on a worldwide scale. With approximately 55,000 employees, we are present in over 200 countries and territories, dedicated to understanding customer needs and offering solutions for individuals and businesses, from small companies to multinationals.

Here, we are committed to Sustainability, focusing on reducing plastic use, addressing climate change issues such as floods, innovating in development policies, and aligning more closely with global changes. We value trust in the digital society and the way we are constantly automated, leveraging technology and strategies to ensure greater security for our information.

We also foster a culture of diversity and inclusion. Our purpose and values are aimed at protecting, inspiring confidence, and helping our employees reach their full potential! We value and defend what is right and promote opportunities for equity among our professionals, regardless of gender, physical disability, LGBTQ+, race, ethnicity, generations, beliefs, etc. We are the first insurer certified with the Stone Wall Certificate. So, if you believe in Diversity as an essential value, Zurich is for you!

We are Certified by GPTW as one of the Best Companies to Work For, for several consecutive years (2018, 2019, 2020, 2022, 2023, and 2024), continuously cultivating our #JeitoZ.

Come be a Zuricher and join our team! Leave your profile in our talent pool!

OUR OPPORTUNITY: Customer Service Operator II

RESPONSIBILITIES:

- Provide courteous, empathetic customer service focused on delivering an excellent experience.

- Quickly and accurately identify customer needs, questions, and requests.

- Provide clear and concise information about products, services, procedures, and insurance coverages.

- Explain contractual terms and conditions accessibly, avoiding excessive technical jargon.

- Ensure data quality and integrity, keeping systems updated.

- Guide customers on next steps, deadlines, and necessary follow-ups.

- Work independently to resolve issues, prioritizing quality standards and targets.

- Demonstrate active listening, collaboration, and effective communication in interactions with customers and team members.

- Adapt swiftly to process, tool, and operational scenario changes.

- Contribute to continuous improvement of service processes.

REQUIREMENTS:

- Enrolled or completed higher education.

- Previous experience in customer service, call centers, or related areas.

- Experience in insurance or financial services is a plus.

- Experience with customer record management in systems.

- Knowledge of insurance products and services (desirable)

HOW WE SUPPORT YOU:

- Welcoming work environment;
- Dress code: Come as You Are!
- 7.5-hour workday.

- Hybrid work model

- UniZurich (our Corporate University);
- Birthday Day Off;

- Z Balance (our health and wellness promotion program);

- University and institutional partnerships;
- Wellhub;
- Medical Assistance (covering spouse and children);
- Dental Assistance (covering spouse and children);
- Nursery/Babysitter Assistance (R$ 502.29 – for children up to 5 years and 11 months);
- Zurichers Club (special benefits on Zurich products);
- Language Live - Platform for English and Spanish courses.
- Parental Leave (regardless of marital status, gender, or sexual orientation, for biological and/or adopted children of any age);
- Life Insurance;
- Profit Sharing (PLR);
- Transportation allowance or commuting reimbursement;
- Private pension plan (contribute up to 6% of your salary, matched by Zurich);
- Meal Voucher – R$ 805.83 per month;
- Meal Allowance – R$ 1,042.60 per month.
- Family Travel Assistance (24 hours);
- Funeral assistance for family members (spouse, children, parents, in-laws);
- Birth Gift Basket: R$ 673.00 for birth-related expenses;
- PreviJúnior, a supplementary pension plan with a one-time contribution of R$ 1,000.00;
- Parents can work remotely during their children’s school holidays (up to 12 years);
- Pet Assistance (dogs and cats): consultations, surgeries, exams, funeral assistance, and more!

LOCATION: São Paulo

de.description:
UNSERE FIRMA

Zurich fördert Vielfalt in all ihren Formen! Wir laden #Frauen, #schwarze Menschen, #Menschen mit Behinderung #PCD, #LGBTQIA+ und #Senioren ein, sich auf unsere Stellen zu bewerben!

Stellen Sie sich vor, Sie arbeiten in einem Unternehmen, das sich wirklich um seine Mitarbeitenden, Kunden, Stakeholder und die gesamte Gemeinschaft kümmert. Stellen Sie sich vor, Sie arbeiten in einem Unternehmen, das sich verpflichtet, das Richtige zu tun, und das zum Ziel hat, der beste Versicherungsanbieter der Welt zu sein!

Zurich ist eines der weltweit führenden Versicherungsunternehmen und eines der wenigen, das auf globaler Ebene tätig ist. Mit etwa 55.000 Mitarbeitenden sind wir in über 200 Ländern und Gebieten vertreten, engagiert, die Bedürfnisse der Kunden zu verstehen und Lösungen für Privatpersonen und Unternehmen anzubieten, von kleinen Firmen bis zu multinationalen Konzernen.

